  "name": "Shiny Pokémon Present Campaign",
  "category": "campaign",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Shiny Pokémon Present Campaign (ポケモンカードゲーム 色ちがいのポケモンプレゼント) was a draw in 2010 for cards with their own illustrations and attacks: two barcodes from packs of HeartGold Collection, SoulSilver Collection, Reviving Legends or Lost Link made one entry, postmarked by 30 June 2010. Course A was shiny Ho-Oh and Lugia and course B shiny Raikou, Entei and Suicune, each for 1,000 winners, and the prizes were to be sent in mid-July 2010. The shiny Legendary Beasts also starred in that summer's film, Zoroark: Master of Illusions. All five were later printed in English in Call of Legends, with SL numbers.",
